dsv41 patch 0076c (draft 22.10.2026, SIDE PATH, not used by production): expert tiles for exllamav3's deterministic
prefill path (_run_prefill_det). Production runs prompt chunks of >= 64 rows through TensorFold's kernels
(VLLM_EXL3_MOE_TF_PROMPT=1 in the recipe launcher's RECIPE_ENV), so this only matters with TF_PROMPT=0.
VLLM_EXL3_MOE_DET_TILE_SLOTS=N: scratch [m*top_k, H] fp32 (480 MiB at 4096 tokens) -> one tile of <= N assignments,
one exl3_moe_gather per tile. Rounding class (tile-wise fp32 association), deterministic.

--- a/vllm_exl3_moe/forward.py	2026-10-22 11:12:43.855116967 +0200
+++ b/vllm_exl3_moe/forward.py	2026-10-22 11:14:41.609514944 +0200
@@ -42,6 +42,16 @@
 # prompts give identical bits run to run; 0 = exllamav3's atomic accumulation (arrival order). Decode is deterministic
 # either way (exl3_smoe / coop).
 _DET_PREFILL = os.environ.get("VLLM_EXL3_MOE_DET_PREFILL", "1") == "1"
+# VLLM_EXL3_MOE_DET_TILE_SLOTS=N (dsv41 patch 0076c, default 0 = off): the deterministic prefill path keeps one fp32 slot
+# per assignment for ALL of a step's assignments, [m * top_k, hidden] fp32 = 480 MiB at 4096 tokens (960 MiB at 8192),
+# the largest single activation of a prefill step's MoE, held by the caching allocator after the first long prompt.
+# With N > 0 and more than N assignments, the physical experts (K-sorted, each group a contiguous range) are cut into
+# tiles of at most N assignments (an expert with more stays whole) and the scratch holds one tile: the tile's experts
+# run with the same kernels and tiers, then one exl3_moe_gather adds the tile's slots in k order into out32. A token
+# whose experts all lie in one tile gets the bits of the untiled path; the others sum their slots tile by tile (other
+# fp32 association, still run-to-run deterministic): rounding class, like 0064. Extra traffic: one out32 read+write per
+# tile (~80 MiB a tile at 4096 tokens), extra launches per tile.
+_DET_TILE = max(0, int(os.environ.get("VLLM_EXL3_MOE_DET_TILE_SLOTS", "0") or 0))
 # VLLM_EXL3_MOE_TF_PROMPT=1: prompt chunks of >= 64 rows through TensorFold's grouped EXL3 kernels (tf_prompt.py):
